## 3. System Architecture Overview

The platform follows a **modular, API-first, multi-tenant SaaS architecture**.

### High-Level Architecture

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                         Client Applications                       │
│   Public Website | Patient Web App | Hospital CRM Web App |       │
│   Super Admin Web App | (Future) Mobile Apps (iOS/Android)        │
└───────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────--┘
                             │  HTTPS / REST (JSON) / WebSockets (chat)
┌───────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────--┐
│                         API Gateway Layer                         │
│   Auth, Rate Limiting, Request Validation, Tenant Resolution      │
└───────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────--┘
                             │
┌───────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────--┐
│                      Application/Service Layer                    │
│  Identity & Auth | Provider Directory | Appointments | Billing    │
│  Medical Records | Pharmacy/Inventory | Notifications | Ads       │
│  Leads | Reviews | Subscriptions | Reporting/Analytics | Audit    │
└───────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────--┘
                             │
┌───────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────--┐
│                        Data & Storage Layer                       │
│   Relational DB (AWS RDS) | Object Storage (documents/images) |   │
│   Cache (session/search) | Search Index (provider discovery)      │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                             │
┌───────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────--┐
│                     External Integrations                         │
│   Payment Gateway (Razorpay) | Email | SMS | WhatsApp Business    │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Architectural Principles

- **API-first:** All frontends (web, future mobile) consume the same versioned REST API. No business logic lives in the frontend.
- **Tenant isolation by design:** Every data-bearing request is scoped by `organization_id` at the query layer, not just the UI layer.
- **Modular services:** Each domain (appointments, billing, records, pharmacy, ads) is a separable module/service boundary, even if deployed as a modular monolith initially — enabling later extraction into microservices.
- **Stateless application servers:** Sessions/tokens are externalized (JWT + refresh token store) so the app tier can scale horizontally.
- **Event-driven notifications:** State changes (appointment confirmed, bill paid, report uploaded) emit events consumed by the notification service, decoupling core transactions from delivery channels (email/SMS/WhatsApp).
- **Extensible by design:** Modules not built in MVP (telemedicine, insurance, AI assistant) are represented as placeholders in the data model/API surface so they can be added without breaking changes.

