## 8. Core Workflows

### 8.1 Patient Journey

```
Register/Login → Search & Compare Providers → View Hospital/Doctor Profile →
Book Appointment → Pay (if required) → Visit Provider → Consultation →
Prescription / Medical Record Generated → Billing/Payment →
Lab/Pharmacy (if required) → Receive Records → Follow-up Reminder →
Return for Future Appointment
```

### 8.2 Appointment Lifecycle

**Booking flow:** Hospital → Department → Doctor → Date → Time Slot → Appointment Type → Confirmation → Payment (if required) → Appointment ID generated → Confirmation sent.

**Status states:**

```
Pending → Confirmed → Checked In → In Consultation → Completed
                    ↘ Cancelled
                    ↘ No Show
```

Hospital staff can transition appointments through these states from the CRM; patients can view live status from the Patient Portal.

### 8.3 Diagnostic Test Booking

```
Search Test → Select Lab → Book Test → Pay → Receive Report
```

### 8.4 Lead-to-Patient Conversion

```
Interest shown (search, profile view, package view) → Lead Created →
New → Contacted → Interested → Appointment Booked → Converted (or Lost)
```

Leads are routed to the relevant hospital/clinic CRM with source tracking (organic, advertisement, referral).

