## 9. Database Architecture

A relational schema (PostgreSQL on AWS RDS) with strict foreign-key integrity and `organization_id`/`tenant_id` scoping on all tenant-owned tables.

### 9.1 Core Entities (representative, not exhaustive)

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `users` | Base identity record (login credentials, role reference) shared across patient/staff/doctor/admin accounts |
| `organizations` | Hospital/clinic/diagnostic-center/pharmacy tenant record, verification status, subscription reference |
| `branches` | Sub-locations under a parent organization |
| `patients` | Patient profile data, linked to `users` |
| `doctors` | Doctor profile, qualifications, specialization, fee, availability, linked to `organizations`/`branches` |
| `staff` | Non-doctor employees, role, department, employee ID, status |
| `departments` | Clinical departments per organization/branch |
| `services` | Billable services offered by an organization |
| `appointments` | Booking record: patient, doctor, department, branch, date/time, status, type |
| `appointment_slots` | Doctor availability/time-slot inventory |
| `medical_records` | Documents, diagnosis, treatment notes, imaging, linked to patient + doctor + organization |
| `prescriptions` / `prescription_items` | Prescription header and line-item medicines/dosage/frequency/duration |
| `lab_reports` | Lab test results linked to patient and diagnostic center |
| `bills` | Invoice header: patient, services, totals, tax, discount, status |
| `payments` | Payment transactions against bills, method, status |
| `medicines` / `inventory` | Pharmacy stock: batch, quantity, purchase/selling price, expiry |
| `health_packages` | Package definition: tests included, price, discount, validity |
| `advertisements` | Ad campaigns: type, status, targeting, performance metrics |
| `leads` | Prospective patient interest records with source/status tracking |
| `reviews` | Ratings and comments on hospitals/clinics/doctors |
| `notifications` | Notification log across in-app/email/SMS/WhatsApp channels |
| `messages` | Patient–provider chat messages, scoped to appointment/organization context |
| `subscriptions` / `subscription_plans` | Organization subscription state and plan catalog |
| `documents` | Generic secure file storage references (S3 keys) with access-control metadata |
| `audit_logs` | Immutable log of sensitive actions (see §10) |
| `roles` / `permissions` | Role definitions and granular permission assignments per organization |

### 9.2 Key Relationships

- `organizations 1—N branches`
- `organizations 1—N doctors, staff, departments, services`
- `patients N—N organizations` (a patient can visit multiple hospitals; each visit history stays scoped to that org, but the patient's own aggregated view is assembled at the API layer for their own portal only)
- `appointments` references `patients`, `doctors`, `departments`, `branches`, `organizations`
- `bills 1—N payments`
- `prescriptions 1—N prescription_items`
- Every tenant-owned table carries `organization_id` (and `branch_id` where applicable) with an indexed foreign key, enforced additionally via row-level security policies.

### 9.3 Indexing Strategy

- Composite indexes on `(organization_id, created_at)` for CRM list views.
- Indexes on `(doctor_id, date, status)` for slot/availability queries.
- Full-text/geo indexes on `organizations`/`doctors` for public search.
- Indexes on foreign keys for all join-heavy relations (`patient_id`, `appointment_id`, `bill_id`).

