## 10. Security & Compliance

| Control | Implementation Approach |
|---|---|
| Authentication | Secure login with hashed passwords (bcrypt/argon2), JWT access + refresh tokens, MFA-ready |
| Authorization | Role-based access control (RBAC) combined with organization-level tenant scoping on every request |
| Session Management | Short-lived access tokens, revocable refresh tokens, forced logout on password change |
| API Security | Authenticated, versioned REST API; input validation and schema enforcement on every endpoint |
| File Upload Validation | Type/size/content validation and virus scanning before storage; documents stored in access-controlled object storage, never served publicly by default |
| Rate Limiting | Applied at the API gateway per user/IP to prevent abuse and brute-force attempts |
| Database Security | Row-Level Security policies keyed on `organization_id`; least-privilege DB credentials per service |
| Encryption | TLS in transit; encryption at rest for the database and object storage; sensitive fields (e.g., identifiers) encrypted at the application layer where warranted |
| Audit Logging | Immutable logs for login/logout, record access, record updates, prescription creation, billing changes, payment changes, staff changes, permission changes, organization changes |
| Public Data Boundaries | Public search/profile pages expose only non-sensitive, provider-controlled marketing data — never patient identities or medical data |

