## 13. Notifications & Communication

### 13.1 Notification Channels
In-app, Email, SMS, and WhatsApp (where supported by the regional provider).

### 13.2 Key Notification Triggers
Appointment confirmation, appointment reminder, appointment cancellation, payment confirmation, prescription available, lab report available, new lead (to organization), new patient (to organization), subscription expiry.

Notifications are emitted as events from core modules and delivered asynchronously by a dedicated notification service, so a slow/failed SMS provider never blocks a core transaction (e.g., booking an appointment).

### 13.3 Communication (Chat) Module
- Secure patient ↔ provider messaging, with history and file sharing.
- Conversations are tied to an appointment/organization context.
- **Access control:** an organization can only see conversations involving its own patients; patients can only see conversations with providers they've engaged.

